 '[{"text":"Thylakoid membrane","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Stroma","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Outer membrane","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Granum stack only","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The Calvin cycle, which fixes CO2 into sugars, takes place in the stroma, the fluid-filled matrix surrounding the thylakoids.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Plant Physiology', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Which plant hormone promotes stomatal closure during water stress?',
 '[{"text":"Auxin","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Gibberellin","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Abscisic acid","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Cytokinin","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Abscisic acid (ABA), often called the stress hormone, promotes stomatal closure to reduce water loss under drought conditions.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Plant Physiology', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'Transpiration in plants occurs mainly through which structure?',
 '[{"text":"Stomata","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Root hairs","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Xylem vessels","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Cuticle only","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The majority of water lost through transpiration exits via the stomata, tiny pores mainly on the leaf surface that also regulate gas exchange.'),

-- Botany: Cell Biology and Genetics
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Cell Biology and Genetics (Plant/General)', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'Which cell organelle is referred to as the "powerhouse of the cell"?',
 '[{"text":"Mitochondria","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Nucleus","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Endoplasmic reticulum","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Lysosome","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Mitochondria generate most of the cell''s ATP through aerobic respiration, earning them the nickname "powerhouse of the cell".'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Cell Biology and Genetics (Plant/General)', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'According to Mendel''s law of segregation, the two alleles of a gene separate from each other during:',
 '[{"text":"Mitosis","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Gamete formation (meiosis)","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Fertilization","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Cell differentiation","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Mendel''s law of segregation states that the two alleles of a gene separate from each other during gamete formation, so each gamete carries only one allele.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Cell Biology and Genetics (Plant/General)', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'DNA replication is best described as being:',
 '[{"text":"Conservative","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Semiconservative","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Dispersive","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Random","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'DNA replication is semiconservative -- each new DNA double helix retains one original (parental) strand and one newly synthesized strand, as demonstrated by the Meselson-Stahl experiment.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Cell Biology and Genetics (Plant/General)', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'The cell wall of plant cells is primarily composed of:',
 '[{"text":"Chitin","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Cellulose","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Peptidoglycan","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Keratin","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
