-- Botany: Ecology and Environment
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Ecology and Environment', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'The flow of energy through an ecosystem, from producers to successive trophic levels, is:',
 '[{"text":"Bidirectional","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Cyclic","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Unidirectional","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Random","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Unlike nutrients, which cycle through an ecosystem, energy flows unidirectionally from producers through successive trophic levels, being progressively lost as heat.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Ecology and Environment', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Which ecological pyramid is always upright, regardless of the ecosystem?',
 '[{"text":"Pyramid of numbers","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Pyramid of biomass","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Pyramid of energy","isCorrect":true},{"text":"None of these is always upright","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'The pyramid of energy is always upright because energy is progressively lost as heat at each trophic transfer, so energy available at each successive level must be less than the level below it.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Ecology and Environment', 'easy', 'mcq',
 'The gradual replacement of one biotic community by another over time in a given area is called:',
 '[{"text":"Ecological succession","isCorrect":true},{"text":"Ecological pyramid","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Biomagnification","isCorrect":false},{"text":"Symbiosis","isCorrect":false}]'::jsonb,
 null, 'Ecological succession is the natural, gradual process by which the species composition of a community changes over time, often progressing toward a stable climax community.'),
('NEET UG', 'Botany', 'Ecology and Environment', 'medium', 'mcq',
 'Biological Oxygen Demand (BOD) is used as a measure of:',
